add('def-dj-bridge-row-column-permutation-modules-and-polytabloids','definition','Hecke row permutation modules and ordinary Dipper–James polytabloids',['def-generic-type-a-hecke-algebra','thm-standard-basis-of-the-generic-type-a-hecke-algebra','def-young-tableau-standard-tableau-and-shape','def-partition-young-diagram-and-conjugate-partition'],r'''Let A=Z[v,v^{-1}] and H=H_v(S_n), (T_i-v)(T_i+1)=0. Use right modules and star(T_w)=T_{w^{-1}}. For a partition lambda set x_lambda=sum_{w in rowYoung(lambda)}T_w and y_lambda=sum_{w in rowYoung(lambda)}(-v)^{-ell(w)}T_w. Define M(lambda)=x_lambda H, with row-standard distinguished-coset vectors x_lambda T_d. Fix row-filled t^lambda and column-filled t_lambda; let w_lambda send t^lambda to t_lambda under the right permutation action. The ordinary DJ polytabloid generator is z_lambda=x_lambda T_{w_lambda}y_{lambda'}, and P(lambda)=z_lambda H inside M(lambda). Define the permutation form by beta(x_lambda T_d,x_lambda T_e)=delta_{d,e}v^{ell(d)} and the standard DJ form as its restriction to P(lambda). Specify empty-shape conventions x=y=z=1. Over a commutative ring R with unit q, define all objects by A→R,v→q; subsequent suppliers must prove freeness, the polytabloid presentation and compatibility with this actual submodule realization.''','Verify coset orientations, length factors and eigenvalues against the concrete DJ construction before scaffolding. Do not DEFINE P(lambda) to be a Murphycell twist; the historical polytabloid submodule/form is the independent side of the required comparison. Prove the permutation-module basis and action directly from standard Hecke multiplication. If the actual cited DJ presentation uses a different canonical w or unit normalization, give the explicit change and update this draft before acceptance; do not silently assume it.')
add('lem-dj-bridge-sign-automorphism-and-star-dual','lemma','The Hecke sign automorphism, pullback and contragredient dual',['def-dj-bridge-row-column-permutation-modules-and-polytabloids','lem-hom-from-a-finite-free-module'],r'''For every R and unit q, theta(T_i)=-q T_i^{-1}=(q-1)-T_i defines an involutive R-algebra automorphism commuting with star. Right-module pullback M^theta has action m*h=m theta(h); the star-contragredient is M^circ=Hom_R(M,R) with (f*h)(m)=f(m h^star). Pullback is exact, preserves submodules, quotients, finite composition multiplicities and simplicity, and commutes with finite-free star-dual and arbitrary base change. At q=1 it is tensoring with sign. theta(x_lambda)=q^{ell(w0_lambda)} y_lambda; this unit factor must be carried through every form comparison.''','Check quadratic and braid relations via generator inverses; check the x/y identity by pairing w with w0_lambda and exact lengths, without division by quantumfactorials. This elementary lemma does not establish Specht duality.')
add('lem-dj-bridge-integral-murphy-and-polytabloid-straightening','lemma','Integral Murphy and polytabloid straightening for the comparison',['def-dj-bridge-row-column-permutation-modules-and-polytabloids','lem-dj-bridge-sign-automorphism-and-star-dual'],r'''Over A, set m_st=T_{d(s)}^star x_lambda T_{d(t)} for standard tableaux s,t of shape lambda. These form a cellular basis with higher dominance ideals I^{>lambda}, fixed-first-index multiplication coefficients and star swapping indices. C_M(lambda)=(x_lambda H+I^{>lambda})/I^{>lambda} is free on m_t=x_lambda T_{d(t)}+I^{>lambda}. Independently, ordinary P(lambda) has a finite standard q-polytabloid basis of cardinal f^lambda, with a split integral inclusion in M(lambda). Establish the exact Garnir relations, all leading unit coefficients, and simultaneous base-change compatibility for both constructions. Define the Murphy form G_lambda by m_us m_tv≡G_lambda(s,t)m_uv mod I^{>lambda}; prove well-definedness, symmetry, star-associativity and finite Gram-kernel submodule property.''','Supply the actual complete integral Garnir proof on BOTH sides. Reuse only published Hecke standard basis and tableau foundations; source20 Murphy/cell prototypes are forbidden dependencies. A generic semisimple rank count cannot prove the integral split inclusion, dominance ideals or singular-parameter basis. This is the main finite straightening prerequisite.')
add('thm-dj-bridge-murphy-cell-is-the-same-shape-specht-dual','theorem','Murphy cells are the same-shape contragredient Specht duals',['lem-dj-bridge-integral-murphy-and-polytabloid-straightening','lem-dj-bridge-sign-automorphism-and-star-dual'],r'''For every commutative R, unit q and partition lambda there is an explicit perfect R-bilinear star-balanced pairing C_M(lambda)×P(lambda)→R, giving C_M(lambda)≅P(lambda)^circ naturally under all coefficient-ring base changes. Equivalently identify the kernel of the row-permutation quotient onto C_M(lambda) with the orthogonal complement of P(lambda), using the independently defined permutation form. The pairing matrix on actual standard bases has determinant a unit in A; its entries and inverse must be given by finite tableau formulas. No nondegeneracy of the form restricted to P(lambda) is required.''','Prove kernel equality integrally and a unit determinant, or an explicit inverse, not merely equal dimensions over Q(v). Distinguish the perfect cross-pairing from either module self-form. The source statements alone do not provide this proof.')
add('thm-dj-bridge-ordinary-specht-is-the-signed-conjugate-murphy-cell','theorem','Ordinary Specht modules and forms match signed conjugate Murphy cells',['thm-dj-bridge-murphy-cell-is-the-same-shape-specht-dual','lem-dj-bridge-integral-murphy-and-polytabloid-straightening','lem-dj-bridge-sign-automorphism-and-star-dual'],r'''For every commutative R, unit q and partition lambda, construct a base-change compatible isomorphism Phi_lambda:P(lambda)→C_M(lambda')^theta. Determine an explicit unit u_lambda(v)∈A^times such that G_{lambda'}(Phi_lambda x,Phi_lambda y)=u_lambda(q) beta_DJ(x,y), for all x,y. Prove the unit and formula in the fixed generator/form normalizations; no unnamed scalar or scalar that may vanish is permitted. Consequently the form radicals and their quotients correspond after every field specialization: D_DJ^lambda≅(D_M^{lambda'})^theta, including zero quotients. Over a PID with a chosen prime, the unit-scaled form identity preserves all Jantzen divisibility submodules and reductions. Also derive P(lambda')≅P(lambda)^circ,theta with the exact position of dual and theta, thereby separating same-shape duality from conjugate-sign transport.''','Supply signed row/column pairing or complete Murphy1995Thm5.2 proof with explicit maps. Compare actual self-forms, not just the abstract modules. COMPUTE u_lambda, do not guess it. theta(x_lambda) carries a quantum-power unit from the preceding lemma. Nonzero form is not equivalent to nonsingular form. If a proposed identity is invalid in these fixed normalizations, expose the precise obstruction before changing claims; root must retain original ordinary-presentation applicability.')
add('cor-dj-bridge-specialization-and-composition-multiplicity-dictionary','corollary','Polytabloid specialization and the exact signed multiplicity dictionary',['thm-dj-bridge-ordinary-specht-is-the-signed-conjugate-murphy-cell','def-integral-specht-lattice-and-base-change','lem-conjugate-specht-sign-duality-over-fields','prop-group-algebra-and-finite-field-specializations-of-the-generic-hecke-algebra'],r'''For every field F at q=1, P(lambda) specializes to the ordinary integral-polytabloid Specht module F⊗S_Z^lambda, with its standard form, and theta becomes sign tensoring. For arbitrary unit q over a field, [P(lambda):D_DJ^mu]=[C_M(lambda'):D_M^{mu'}] whenever D_M^{mu'} is nonzero. For a Schur corner already proved to send W(lambda) to C_M(lambda) and L(lambda) to D_M(lambda), the ordinary dictionary is F(W(lambda'))≅P(lambda)^theta and F(L(lambda'))≅(D_DJ^lambda)^theta, including zero; it is never the untwisted conjugate-dual identity. The simultaneous-twist multiplicities agree. No Schur algebra or source20 convention result is a prerequisite for this conditional dictionary.''','At q1 show each concrete q-polytabloid and permutation form specializes to its integral tabloid counterpart; no complex-only standard-polytabloid theorem is extended to arbitraryfields. Multiplicity equality follows by the exact theta pullback. Schur assertions are conditional applications of the proved bridge, not a backward dependency on source20.')
